    "background_story": "Thomas was a brilliant and eccentric scientist who had spent his entire career studying the mysteries of cryogenics. His life's work was centered around the development of a revolutionary cryoscope, a device capable of freezing and preserving living tissues at incredibly low temperatures. Thomas's obsession with cryogenics began when his wife passed away, and he became determined to find a way to preserve human life. Years of tireless work and experimentation finally paid off when he successfully tested his cryoscope on a small mammal. The scientific community hailed Thomas as a pioneer, and his invention opened up new possibilities for medical research and life extension. Though his work was groundbreaking, Thomas's personal motivations remained rooted in his desire to one day revive his beloved wife, frozen in time, awaiting the day when science could bring her back to him.",
